-*   **Color Priors:**
-    *   $C(r)$: Ground truth color from the input view for ray $r$.
-    *   $C_l(r)$: Color of the corresponding pixel in the 2D inpainted image generated by LaMa for ray $r$ [S1].
-    *   $\hat{C}_c(r), \hat{C}_f(r)$: Predicted coarse and fine colors for ray $r$ from the NeRF [S1].
+*   **NeRF Network:** Standard MLP taking 3D position $\mathbf{x}$ and viewing direction $\mathbf{d}$, outputting density $\sigma$ and color $\mathbf{c}$. The method assumes a coarse and fine network structure, denoted as $\hat{C}_c$ and $\hat{C}_f$ [S1].
